      "itemDescription": "The largest mutual life insurance provider by revenue in the U.S. came in 71st on the Fortune 500 after a year of steady growth.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>The insurance provider paid out a $2 billion dividend to clients in 2023, the largest in company history.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>CEO Craig DeSanto started his role as chief executive in April 2022, replacing Ted Mathas.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>The company reported $58.5 billion in revenue in 2022, up 14% from the year prior.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>New York Life saw a significant drop in profits, however, reporting a loss of more than $1 billion in 2022, as many insurance providers faced higher claims amid rising inflation.</li><br />\r\n</ul>",
